## Creating columns: `mutate`

You can create new columns using `mutate` verb to add more information in your data frame. 

For example, we want to add a new column called `gdp` that will be the result of multiplying the population (`pop`) by `gpdPercap`. 

```{r}
gapminder %>% 
  mutate(
    gdp = pop * gdpPercap
  ) %>% 
  select(pop, gdpPercap, gdp)
```

